{
 "about": "Past stuck defects with the fix that closed them, for scoring the stuck lookup without a model (plan HK.4; scripts/loop/replay_lookups.py). `error` is the line a lookup searches; `names_the_fix` holds patterns (case-insensitive), any one of which in the note a fixer is shown means it names the known fix; `public` is false where the line itself names no cause, so no public answer could. `measured_in` is the fix-log row or plan item that recorded the case. Target: at least 60% of the public cases named. `workspace` is what the case's project held when its error was met, laid out under an empty workspace before the lookup is asked (path from the workspace root: the file's text, or a JSON value written as JSON): the dependency gate's record and the stack facts for the packages the project declared, at the releases it ran (versions and dates read from each registry on 2026-11-25), and, where the error says a package has no such name, the installed package's files cut to the declarations the answer reads.",
